cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "all-research-skills: research tooling skills"
message: "If you use this skill, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucchesi
    given-names: Alessandro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0624-5311"
    affiliation: "IRST \"Dino Amadori\" IRCCS, Meldola, Italy"
abstract: >-
  A collection of research tooling skills. The first, scientific-figures,
  compiles a declarative specification into journal-ready vector
  figures for scientific manuscripts. Relations carry a mandatory evidence
  level rendered through a dedicated visual channel, so a proposed mechanism
  cannot be drawn as a demonstrated one; pictorial assets resolve against a
  registry of open-licensed libraries under an enforced licence gate; and
  type size is treated as a hard constraint at the target column width.
keywords:
  - scientific illustration
  - graphical abstract
  - mechanism of action
  - pathway diagram
  - reproducible figures
  - open licensing
license: MIT
version: 0.7.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
